    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"AFS and PES in settlements\"\ndescription: \"Dominicis et al. (2023) as the reference study for SO4, the 38 studies compared (identified by location, target group, arrangement and DOI) and the gaps identified in the literature\"\npage-layout: full\ntoc: false\n---\n\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"faixa-versao\">\nPreliminary version for the project team. The table only identifies each study (location, biome, target group, arrangement and DOI) and gives no numerical results.\n English translation under review. If the two versions differ, the Portuguese text prevails.\n</div>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## The reference study\n\nThe study by Dominicis et al. (2023), published in *Forests* ([10.3390/f14102110](https://doi.org/10.3390/f14102110)), assesses the financial viability of agroforestry systems (AFS) established by family farmers, most of them agrarian-reform settlers, in the Descoberto River basin (Federal District, Cerrado). The authors compare results with and without payment for environmental services (PES), using indicators such as net present value (NPV) and internal rate of return (IRR).\n\nThe specific objective on bioeconomic scenarios (SO4) will replicate and extend this design in the project's three pilot areas, one in each biome. The search for similar studies serves a dual purpose: to inform the choice of methods and to show what is still missing from the literature.\n\n## The 38 studies compared\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"kpi-grade\">\n<div class=\"kpi\">\n<div class=\"kpi-rotulo\">Studies compared</div>\n<div class=\"kpi-valor\">38</div>\n<div class=\"kpi-meta\">Oct 2026 search</div>\n<div class=\"kpi-comp\">30 with a DOI checked against Crossref</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"kpi\">\n<div class=\"kpi-rotulo\">In the Amazon</div>\n<div class=\"kpi-valor\">18</div>\n<div class=\"kpi-meta\">studies that mention this biome</div>\n<div class=\"kpi-comp\">including studies covering both the Amazon and the Cerrado</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"kpi\">\n<div class=\"kpi-rotulo\">In the Cerrado</div>\n<div class=\"kpi-valor\">11</div>\n<div class=\"kpi-meta\">studies that mention this biome</div>\n<div class=\"kpi-comp\">including transition zones</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"kpi\">\n<div class=\"kpi-rotulo\">In the Pantanal</div>\n<div class=\"kpi-valor\">0</div>\n<div class=\"kpi-meta\">studies solely on the Pantanal</div>\n<div class=\"kpi-comp\">1 in the transition zone with the Cerrado</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"kpi\">\n<div class=\"kpi-rotulo\">Outside Brazil</div>\n<div class=\"kpi-valor\">4</div>\n<div class=\"kpi-meta\">studies from other countries</div>\n<div class=\"kpi-comp\">payment for environmental services and carbon</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\nThe table below identifies each study only by its location and biome, target group, arrangement and digital object identifier (DOI). To find a study, use the search box or the biome filter.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"reactable html-widget html-fill-item\" id=\"tab-saf\" style=\"width:auto;height:auto;\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"tab-saf\">{\"x\":{\"tag\":{\"name\":\"Reactable\",\"attribs\":{\"data\":{\"Estudo\":[\"Dominicis et al. 2023\",\"Rodrigues et al. 2007\",\"Rodrigues et al. 2008\",\"Silva et al. 2018\",\"Solidaridad 2021\",\"Sousa et al. 2019\",\"Paraense et al. 2022\",\"Soares et al. 2026\",\"Francez and Rosa 2011\",\"Tremblay et al. 2014\",\"Santana et al. 2023\",\"Marques et al. 2017\",\"Queiroz et al. 2020\",\"Menezes et al. 2005\",\"RECA Project (Embrapa, 2016 panel)\",\"Palma et al. 2020\",\"Garcia et al. 2021\",\"Paulus et al. 2021\",\"Agostinho et al. 2022\",\"Pagiola et al. 2007; NPV in Pagiola et al. 2004\",\"Gobbi and Casasola 2003\",\"Ribeiro et al. 2007\",\"Silva and Cunha 2013\",\"Hespanhol et al. 2026\",\"Ferreira et al. 2024\",\"Castro Neto 