rget\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener\"},\"children\":[\"10.1038/s41467-023-43861-4\"]}]}]},{\"name\":\"Fragment\",\"attribs\":[],\"children\":[{\"name\":\"Fragment\",\"attribs\":[],\"children\":[{\"name\":\"a\",\"attribs\":{\"href\":\"https://doi.org/10.1088/1748-9326/ab7f0d\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener\"},\"children\":[\"10.1088/1748-9326/ab7f0d\"]}]}]},{\"name\":\"Fragment\",\"attribs\":[],\"children\":[{\"name\":\"Fragment\",\"attribs\":[],\"children\":[{\"name\":\"a\",\"attribs\":{\"href\":\"https://doi.org/10.1590/01047760201521031658\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener\"},\"children\":[\"10.1590/01047760201521031658\"]}]}]},\"—\",\"—\",{\"name\":\"Fragment\",\"attribs\":[],\"children\":[{\"name\":\"Fragment\",\"attribs\":[],\"children\":[{\"name\":\"a\",\"attribs\":{\"href\":\"https://doi.org/10.3390/f16060978\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener\"},\"children\":[\"10.3390/f16060978\"]}]}]},\"—\",{\"name\":\"Fragment\",\"attribs\":[],\"children\":[{\"name\":\"Fragment\",\"attribs\":[],\"children\":[{\"name\":\"a\",\"attribs\":{\"href\":\"https://doi.org/10.1017/s1742170519000280\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener\"},\"children\":[\"10.1017/s1742170519000280\"]}]},{\"name\":\"Fragment\",\"attribs\":[],\"children\":[\"; \",{\"name\":\"a\",\"attribs\":{\"href\":\"https://doi.org/10.3389/fsufs.2025.1518747\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener\"},\"children\":[\"10.3389/fsufs.2025.1518747\"]}]}]},{\"name\":\"Fragment\",\"attribs\":[],\"children\":[{\"name\":\"Fragment\",\"attribs\":[],\"children\":[{\"name\":\"a\",\"attribs\":{\"href\":\"https://doi.org/10.3390/su9010158\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener\"},\"children\":[\"10.3390/su9010158\"]}]}]},{\"name\":\"Fragment\",\"attribs\":[],\"children\":[{\"name\":\"Fragment\",\"attribs\":[],\"children\":[{\"name\":\"a\",\"attribs\":{\"href\":\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.landusepol.2024.107122\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener\"},\"children\":[\"10.1016/j.landusepol.2024.107122\"]}]}]},\"—\"],\"minWidth\":160,\"style\":{\"fontSize\":\"0.78rem\",\"wordBreak\":\"break-all\"}}],\"filterable\":true,\"searchable\":true,\"pagination\":false,\"defaultPageSize\":38,\"striped\":true,\"compact\":true,\"language\":{\"searchPlaceholder\":\"Search study, location, target group or arrangement\",\"noData\":\"No studies found\"},\"elementId\":\"tab-saf\",\"dataKey\":\"ecee14073d4f69d80c2516a58299ec16\"},\"children\":[]},\"class\":\"reactR_markup\"},\"evals\":[\"tag.attribs.columns.2.filterMethod\",\"tag.attribs.columns.2.filterInput.attribs.onChange\"],\"jsHooks\":[]}</script>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n- [Download the 38 studies (CSV)](../../arquivos/literatura/resa_estudos_saf_psa_oe4.csv) · [data dictionary](../../arquivos/literatura/dicionarios/resa_estudos_saf_psa_oe4.csv)\n\n::: {.nota-fonte}\nSource: compiled by the authors from the search for studies similar to Dominicis et al. (2023), RESA Project (15 and 16 October 2026). Notes: each study's biome is the one indicated for its location. DOIs were matched by first author and year, and only where there was a single record checked against Crossref. A study made up of more than one work therefore has more than one DOI. The DOI for Lucchesi et al. (2024) was checked separately against Crossref on 19 October 2026. A missing DOI does not mean the work is unpublished, since reports and technical literature generally have no DOI. Where the source does not state the location or target group, the cell reads \"not stated\".\n:::\n\n## Gaps in the literature\n\nComparing the studies points to five gaps in the literature. The project treats them differently, depending on the status assigned to each: three are confirmed, one is partly filled and one is not asserted. The first two, both confirmed, concern geographical coverage. The search found no viability study of AFS or productive restoration in a settlement in Mato Grosso (gap 1), and the studies conducted in the state deal with smallholdings outside settlements, commercial farms or experiments. Nor did it find any such study in the Pantanal (gap 2), so the closest parameters come from the Cerrado of Mato Grosso do Sul, in the transition zone with the Pantanal.\n\nGap 3, on valuing carbon at market prices in settlements and small-scale production, is partly filled. Some studies include carbon in the cash flow of small producers, although most were conducted outside Brazil; in Brazil itself, cases are few and partial. By contrast, gap 4, on treating PES, carbon, risk and differences between families together in the same study, is confirmed, as no study combines all four elements. This combination is therefore SO4's contribution.\n\nFinally, gap 5, on land credit debt in the cash flow, is not asserted. The search did not target this point, which is relevant to the N. Sra. Aparecida case (land credit). A dedicated search is therefore needed before this gap can be asserted.\n\n::: {.nota-fonte}\nSource: compiled by the authors from the RESA Project's synthesis of the October 2026 search, set out in a separate text.\n:::\n",
